# Pages, config and public assets

- `src/pages.mjs` exports the five routes (`''`, `guide/`, `privacy/`, `support/`, `terms/`); `scripts/build.mjs` adds the shared head (meta CSP, referrer policy), header and footer. Never add a page outside that list without updating `build.mjs`, `check.mjs`, tests and `verify-live.mjs`. The extension links to `/`, `/guide/`, `/privacy/` and `/support/` under `/audivoya/`: never rename or remove them.
- Internal links: `url('<route>')` (prefixes `site.base`). External links: HTTPS with `${ext}` (`target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`). Email: `${mail}`.
- Forbidden in output: `<form>`, `<input>`, `<iframe>`, inline `<script>`, `on*=` attributes, remote fonts, CDNs, analytics, embeds, cookies. Progressive enhancement lives only in `public/assets/site.js`; every page must work without it.
- Ids are unique per page; every `#anchor` and `/audivoya/…#anchor` must exist (check.mjs).
- Dynamic text goes through `escapeText`. Templates are long single lines: change the smallest span, never reflow neighbouring copy.
- Facts are data, never literals: version `site.extensionVersion`, stores `site.stores.*`, email `site.email`, language count and names from `languageCatalog` (`src/languages.json`).
- `site.config.mjs`: `extensionVersion` is the version **live in the stores**; `stores.*` are anonymously verified listing URLs; both change only in a release-sync Phase B PR. `updated` (YYYY-MM-DD) is the sitemap lastmod.
- `src/languages.json` is a byte copy of the extension's `docs/release/chrome-store/languages.json`; never hand-edit it. The "checked <date>" sentence in `supportedLanguages` follows its `verifiedOn`.
- Privacy and terms carry "Last updated <Month D, YYYY>" in their intro: move it whenever their content changes.
- Copy rules: English; plain and specific; disclose delay, Google API fees, DRM/protected-media limits and same-profile key storage limits; no banned claims (`BYOK`, `100% secure`, `zero latency`, `millisecond translation`, `unlimited dubbing`, `trusted by <n>`), no retired brand "Realtime Dubbing". Review with site-content.
- Images: self-hosted under `public/assets/`, < 3 MB, `width`/`height` equal to the intrinsic pixel size, `loading="lazy"` below the fold, meaningful `alt` (empty `alt=""` only for decoration).
- Generated assets — never hand-edit: `public/assets/guide/*.png` and `capture.json` (`scripts/capture-guide.mjs`, site-capture), `public/assets/social-card.png` (`scripts/generate-social-card.mjs`). One capture branch at a time.
- `public/assets/site.css` is a hot file: no horizontal overflow at 320 px and 640 px, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, never make colour the only state signal.
- Hot files to claim: `src/pages.mjs`, `site.config.mjs`, `public/assets/site.css`, `public/assets/guide`.
- Verify: `npm run check`, `npm run test:e2e`, `npm run build && node scripts/capture-preview.mjs` and review `artifacts/*.png`; prepend a `docs/VALIDATION.md` entry.
